{"book":{"id":"book-had-it-coming-robyn-doolittle","slug":"had-it-coming-robyn-doolittle","title":"Had It Coming","authors":[{"id":"person-robyn-doolittle","name":"Robyn Doolittle"}],"isbn13":["9780735236592"],"subjects":["True Crime & Justice"],"topics":["Crime, Policing & Violence","Essays & Cultural Criticism","Housing, Cities & Urban Life"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Had%20It%20Coming%20Robyn%20Doolittle","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Had%20It%20Coming%20Robyn%20Doolittle","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Had%20It%20Coming%20Robyn%20Doolittle","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Had%20It%20Coming%20Robyn%20Doolittle","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28427191M"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-rbc-taylor-nonfiction-wikipedia-rbc-taylor-prize-winners-and-finalists","source-open-library-had-it-coming-robyn-doolittle"],"publicationYear":2019,"pageCount":292,"summary":"\"An illuminating, timely look at the changing landscape of sexual politics by a popular journalist. For nearly two years, Globe and Mail reporter Robyn Doolittle investigated how Canadian police handle sexual assault cases. Her findings were shocking: across the country, in big cities and small towns, the system was dismissing a high number of allegations as \"unfounded.\" A police officer would simply view the claim as baseless and no investigation would follow. Of the 26,500 reported cases of sexual assault in 2015, only 1,400 resulted in convictions. The response to Doolittle's groundbreaking Unfounded series was swift.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10323611-L.jpg","displaySummary":"For nearly two years, Globe and Mail reporter Robyn Doolittle investigated how Canadian police handle sexual assault cases. Her findings were shocking: across the country, in big cities and small towns, the system was dismissing a high number of allegations as \"unfounded.\" A police offic